Third-party data and documents
------------------------------

This MIT license covers the original source code, documentation, and derived
artifacts authored for this repository. It does NOT re-license any third-party
data or documents that are redistributed or referenced here. In particular:

* Public geospatial layers (USGS 3DEP DEM, Esri NLCD fractional imperviousness,
  NHDPlus HR hydrography, NYC DEP stormwater polygons, NYC 311 complaints,
  USGS Hurricane Ida high-water marks, FEMA Sandy surge inundation, NYC
  FloodNet events and sensor metadata) remain under the terms of their
  respective publishers and Open Data licenses. See `data/raw/DATA_SOURCES.md`
  and the per-directory `DOWNLOAD_MANIFEST.json` files for source URLs,
  retrieval dates, and license notes.
* The files `1-s2.0-S2212420926001032-main.pdf` and
  `1-s2.0-S2212420926001032-main.md` are a copy of a third-party published
  journal article (Elsevier / IJDRR) included for offline literature-review
  and citation-caveat reference only. They are NOT covered by the MIT license,
  are NOT redistributed with any claim of ownership, and should be replaced by
  a DOI link (or removed) before any further redistribution. Copyright remains
  with the original publisher and authors.
